# How to cite xisfconv. GitHub shows this as "Cite this repository".
# The version below is that of include/xisfconv.h: the tests hold the two against each other.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use xisfconv in work that you publish, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "xisfconv: a converter between PixInsight XISF, FITS and ASDF images, and its library libxisfconv"
abstract: >-
  xisfconv converts astronomical images between PixInsight XISF, FITS and ASDF in every direction,
  with their keywords, astrometric solutions and XISF properties, reads the raw images of DNG
  files, exports TIFF and PNG, rewrites
  the storage of XISF files and verifies files. The same code is a library with a C API,
  libxisfconv, and a Python package that reads and writes the images as NumPy arrays.
authors:
  - family-names: Kobierczynski
    given-names: Jurgen
version: 0.20.0
date-released: "2026-10-09"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jkobierczynski/xisfconv"
url: "https://github.com/jkobierczynski/xisfconv"
license:
  - GPL-3.0-or-later
  - LGPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - astrophotography
  - XISF
  - PixInsight
  - FITS
  - ASDF
  - DNG
  - WCS
